 @bruuunchiii  2070 super was a refresh card though and released almost a year after the 20-series launch. So managing the same improvement right from the get go is better. 
Plus you have to keep in mind the cost of the card it is matching. The 1080ti was a 700 bucks card while the 2080ti was 1000 or rather 1200 bucks. Now of course the 2080ti was overpriced but just because the card should have been 700 bucks doesn't change the fact that you had to pay 1200. 

So it is very obvious why people are/were excited. A level of perfomance which was out of their reach prior to the 3000 series is now within their budget.

 @choatus  The AMD release will likely not mirror that of Nvidia's. They have a different silicon manufacturer (TSMC vs Samsung) and will not have the same incentive to hold off on supply (just a theory on Nvidia scarcity).

Also, regarding AMD & miners, it appears you are extrapolating a bit. Firstly, it's just a rumor about XFX. Videocards has been wrong before so they are not infallible. Second, if this were true, they are referring to older cards such as Polaris / GCN and RDNA 1, not the new cards this year RDNA 2. It's just another big jump to believe this article and to believe that miners are already betting on the new AMD cards and to believe all AIBs will do the same as XFX for RDNA 2 in this scenario.

It's just not likely.

 @choatus  Mr. Choatus, I literally did that. You seemed to jump to the conclusion or didn't read my statement correctly.

I was careful to ensure that my claim of likelihood of lessened supply issues came from three sources: a) a rumor tech tuber, b) a VP at AMD and c) my understanding of wafer supply from 2019/2020 TSMC reservations. It seems that I should've switched up the order in which I relayed this to ensure better absorption of my point.

It would be a pretty hypocritical 'conservative' stance to cast aspersions then base my claims on the same. However, you don't know me, so I get that. Also, Moore's law has been getting better at his predictions through (claimed) pruning of accurate sources, which is why I put him in my list. He's not infallible and has definitely been wrong before. I trust Adored a bit less, plus he's exiting the rumor mill game. His emotions seem to drive his analysis moreso.

