 @dralord1307  Since when is having charisma/humor the antithesis of being very intelligent? Keep in mind that GamersNexus does MORE comedic and charismatic stuff than Jay (i.e poking fun at Nvidia and Intel), yet GamersNexus is the MOST detailed tech channel of them all. Hardware Unboxed has the charisma of a cardboard box. I'm sorry but the persona of the presenter(s) DOES matter, and this channel lacks it. The most charismatic thing they have is one dude has a 80s pornstar mustache for the last 4 months - big whoop. 

Say what you want, but Jay routinely makes educational videos about what-if scenarios such as overclocking and bottle-necking. That's not even factoring in the custom PC builds and product reviews he uploads. Jay has a wider net of content overall, and that's really not up for debate. This channel is 80% rambling/speculating about tech rumors and 20% product reviews. THAT is why Jay has almost 3M subscribers and this channel is barely touching half a Mil. "HEY! Jay started YouTube 3 years earlier!" - this channel has had half a decade to not even catch up, but just reach HALF the subscriber count of Jay and they've failed. 

